<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narasa Nayaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1503</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narasa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaka</a> was a general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishnadevaraya">Krishnadevaraya</a>. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saluva-narasimha">Saluva Narasimha</a> he acted as regent for the young Saluva heir and was the real ruler of the empire from about 1491 until his death in 1503, campaigning against the Bahmani successor states and in the south. His son Vira Narasimha founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuluva-dynasty">Tuluva dynasty</a>.</p></div>
